[Eb7] Lord, I'm coming [Ab] home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] I've wasted many [Db] precious [Ab] years,
Now I'm coming [Eb7] home;
I [Ab] now repent with [Db] bitter [Ab] tears,
[Eb7] Lord, I'm coming [Ab] home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] I'm tired of sin and [Db] straying, [Ab] Lord,
Now I'm coming [Eb7] home;
I'll [Ab] trust Thy love, be-[Db] lieve Thy [Ab] Word,
[Eb7] Lord, I'm coming [Ab] home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
My [Ab] only hope, my [Db] only [Ab] plea,
Now I'm coming [Eb7] home;
That [Ab] Jesus died, and [Db] died for [Ab] me,
